@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1784 = private unnamed_addr constant [1203 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `tarfile.extractall`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A\0AExtracting archives from untrusted sources without prior inspection is\0Aa security risk, as maliciously crafted archives may contain files that\0Awill be written outside of the target directory. For example, the archive\0Acould include files with absolute paths (e.g., `/etc/passwd`), or relative\0Apaths with parent directory references (e.g., `../etc/passwd`).\0A\0AOn Python 3.12 and later, use `filter='data'` to prevent the most dangerous\0Asecurity issues (see: [PEP 706]). On earlier versions, set the `members`\0Aargument to a trusted subset of the archive's members.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport tarfile\0Aimport tempfile\0A\0Atar = tarfile.open(filename)\0Atar.extractall(path=tempfile.mkdtemp())\0Atar.close()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-22](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html)\0A- [Python documentation: `TarFile.extractall`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/tarfile.html#tarfile.TarFile.extractall)\0A- [Python documentation: Extraction filters](https://docs.python.org/3/library/tarfile.html#tarfile-extraction-filter)\0A\0A[PEP 706]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0706/#backporting-forward-compatibility\0A", align 1
@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1785 = private unnamed_addr constant [30 x i8] c"Uses of `tarfile.extractall()`", align 1
@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1786 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ ptr, [8 x i8] }> <{ ptr @anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1785, [8 x i8] c"\1E\00\00\00\00\00\00\00" }>, align 8
@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1787 = private unnamed_addr constant [566 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for single-element tuples in exception handlers (e.g.,\0A`except (ValueError,):`).\0A\0ANote: Single-element tuples consisting of a starred expression\0Aare allowed.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA tuple with a single element can be more concisely and idiomatically\0Aexpressed as a single value.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept (ValueError,):\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept ValueError:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `except` clause](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#except-clause)\0A", align 1
