@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1860 = private unnamed_addr constant [746 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `.values` on Pandas Series and Index objects.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `.values` attribute is ambiguous as its return type is unclear. As\0Asuch, it is no longer recommended by the Pandas documentation.\0A\0AInstead, use `.to_numpy()` to return a NumPy array, or `.array` to return a\0APandas `ExtensionArray`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Aanimals = pd.read_csv(\22animals.csv\22).values  # Ambiguous.\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pandas as pd\0A\0Aanimals = pd.read_csv(\22animals.csv\22).to_numpy()  # Explicit.\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Pandas documentation: Accessing the values in a Series or Index](https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/stable/whatsnew/v0.24.0.html#accessing-the-values-in-a-series-or-index)\0A", align 1
