@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1863 = private unnamed_addr constant [654 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for functions with \22dunder\22 names (that is, names with two\0Aleading and trailing underscores) that are not documented.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends that only documented \22dunder\22 methods are used:\0A\0A> ...\22magic\22 objects or attributes that live in user-controlled\0A> namespaces. E.g. `__init__`, `__import__` or `__file__`. Never invent\0A> such names; only use them as documented.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef __my_function__():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef my_function():\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.ignore-names`\0A- `lint.pep8-naming.extend-ignore-names`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/\0A", align 1
