@anon.6aa2d360734573fdde4b4ffe4a284ba1.1881 = private unnamed_addr constant [628 x i8] c"## Removed\0AThis rule is identical to [G010] which should be used instead.\0A\0A## What it does\0ACheck for usages of the deprecated `warn` method from the `logging` module.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `warn` method is deprecated. Use `warning` instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0A\0Adef foo():\0A    logging.warn(\22Something happened\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0A\0Adef foo():\0A    logging.warning(\22Something happened\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `logger.Logger.warning`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/logging.html#logging.Logger.warning)\0A\0A[G010]: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/logging-warn/\0A", align 1
